# UI usability (sort / search / navigate / understand / look alike)

Apply when **adding, changing, or reviewing** any user-visible UI in `sqyre-app` or `sqyre-overlay` (desktop, wasm editor, overlays, trays, dialogs, pickers, tooltips). Prefer existing helpers over one-off widgets.

**Agent behavior:** if a change or existing panel violates these principles, **warn and suggest** a concrete fix — do not refuse the work or invent large refactors unless asked. When touching a list/panel, briefly audit neighbors in the same surface.

Audience: **casual automation beginners first**. Power-user / technical controls go behind a collapsed **Advanced** (or equivalent) section when possible — prefer [`tip_advanced`](crates/sqyre-app/src/action_tooltip/sections.rs).

## Principles

### Sortable
- Named lists (macros, items, programs, coords, tags, …) present a **stable, predictable order** (usually display-name, case-insensitive).
- If order matters to the user, expose an obvious control (column header, sort menu, or existing domain sort) — do not rely on insertion order alone.
- Reuse `macro_meta::cmp_display_name` (macros) / `pickers::sort_by_display_name` (name/id rows) rather than ad-hoc sorts that disagree across panels.

### Searchable
- Any list that can grow beyond ~a screenful needs a **filter field** with `hint_text` (what to type) and case-insensitive match on the labels users see.
- Prefer `widgets::searchable_combo` / `searchable_combo_with` for growing dropdowns; for free lists mirror the macro-list filter (`ui_macro_list.rs`) or the command-palette query.
- Empty / no-match bodies: `widgets::list_vacancy` / `empty_state` — never a blank void.

### Navigable (local first)
- Prefer **in-panel** keyboard behavior over new global chords. Do not steal keys while recording macros/hotkeys/chords.
- Default local list/dialog keys (when focus is in that surface):
  - **↑ / ↓** — move selection
  - **Enter** — activate / confirm primary action
  - **Esc** — cancel / close / clear selection as appropriate
  - **type-to-filter** when a search field exists (focus it on open when that is the main job, e.g. command palette)
- Keep mouse/click paths complete; keyboard is additive accessibility, not the only way.
- Mirror proven patterns: `widgets::consume_escape` (Esc closes the topmost layer only — never raw `consume_key(Escape)`), `poll_confirm_keys`, `save_cancel_row` / `confirm_window`, command palette, `var_pills`.

### Usable
- Primary actions are visible buttons/menus — not gesture- or hotkey-only.
- Destructive actions need a clear confirm (existing pending-delete / dialog patterns).
- One obvious next step on empty states (“No macros yet — create one”).
- Avoid requiring the user to know IDs, paths, or enum variant names to complete common tasks.

### Understandable
- Labels and hints use everyday words (macro, item, click, wait) — not crate/type jargon in the UI string.
- Every non-obvious control gets hover help or a one-line hint.
- Errors and status text say what happened and what to try next in plain language.
- Progressive disclosure: show the common path first; tuck thresholds, preprocess flags, gate formulas, etc. under Advanced.

### Consistent rendering (look alike / refactorable)
Keep surfaces **visually interchangeable**: same control kinds should look and lay out the same so refactors stay safe and screenshots/docs stay reliable.

- **Compose shared primitives** — `theme::*` (colors, framed sections, overlays), `widgets::*` (icon/controls, fields, dialogs, headers, tags), `pickers::*`, `tip_section` / `tip_wrapped_section` / `tip_advanced`. Do not copy-paste one-off spacing, strokes, or button chrome.
- **No local palettes** — use `theme::PRIMARY`, `MACRO_START`, `MACRO_STOP`, `accent_dim`, `overlay_panel_fill`, `contrast_fg`, and egui `TextStyle` / `ui.visuals()`. Avoid hard-coded `Color32::from_rgb(…)` in panel code unless adding a token in `sqyre-ui-theme` (shared with overlay) or `sqyre-app/src/theme/tokens.rs` (app-only).
- **Stable geometry** — prefer shared widths (`W_TEXT`, `W_VAR`), `fit_dialog_window` / `fit_dialog_popup` / `fill_resize_body`, and `dialog_scroll`. Obey [egui-window-size-ratchet](egui-window-size-ratchet.mdc); do not invent per-panel size math that drifts.
- **Match the nearest sibling** — new rows, toolbars, lists, and confirm footers should mirror an adjacent panel of the same kind (same icon size, gap, weak-count suffix, Save/Cancel row). Visual novelty needs an explicit product ask.
- **Extract on repeat** — if the same layout appears twice, lift it into `widgets` / `theme` / `tip_*` instead of diverging copies (easier refactors, fewer look bugs).
- **Predictable density** — reuse existing section gaps and `horizontal_wrapped` patterns from tip sections; do not mix dense custom grids next to standard framed sections without cause.

### Accessible (AccessKit is on via eframe defaults)
- Icon-only buttons use `widgets::icon_button(ui, glyph, tip)`, which sets an AccessKit label. Custom-painted widgets call `response.widget_info(|| WidgetInfo::labeled(..))`; a glyph is not a label (screen readers and `egui_kittest` `get_by_label` depend on it).
- Do not signal state by color alone; pair with icon/text. Text on custom fills uses `contrast_fg(bg)`.
- Request focus once on open (track a flag), not every frame; keep Tab order = add order.

### Immediate-mode hygiene
- Stable IDs: `id_salt(..)` on ScrollArea/ComboBox/CollapsingHeader inside loops; `ui.push_id(domain_id, ..)`, never a row index (sort/filter shifts state).
- No per-frame disk I/O, image decode, or large sorts/filters — cache and invalidate on change.
- Prefer `request_repaint_after(d)`; unconditional `request_repaint()` only while animating or a run is active.

## Checklist (new or touched UI)

- [ ] List/combo: sorted predictably; filter or searchable combo if the set can grow
- [ ] Empty / no-match states have plain copy
- [ ] Local ↑↓ / Enter / Esc (or documented why not) without breaking record modes
- [ ] Beginner path visible; advanced options collapsed by default
- [ ] Labels, hints, and errors readable by a non-technical user
- [ ] Reused `theme::*` tokens/visuals, `widgets::*` (incl. controls), `pickers::*`, `tip_*` / `tip_advanced` (no one-off chrome/colors)
- [ ] Layout matches a sibling of the same kind; dialogs use shared fit/scroll helpers
- [ ] Icon/custom widgets labeled; stable ids in loops; no heavy per-frame work

## Out of scope unless asked

- New **global** application hotkey schemes (local panel keys first)
- Brand / theme redesigns (changing the look system itself) — consistency with the *current* system is in scope
